    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Aspects (abnormal in red)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Bones / soft tissue: rib fractures, lytic lesions, "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       },
       {
        "type": "highlight",
        "attrs": {
         "hex": "FF0000"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "rib notching"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", subQ air"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Chest x-ray: a "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       },
       {
        "type": "highlight",
        "attrs": {
         "hex": "FF0000"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "“3” sign"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " in the upper left mediastinal shadow; heart size is normal unless heart failure supervenes"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Dilated intercostal collateral arteries may erode the 3rd to 8th ribs, causing "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       },
       {
        "type": "highlight",
        "attrs": {
         "hex": "FF0000"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "rib notching"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ", seldom seen before age 5 years"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 6,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Causes"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "A localized narrowing of the lumen, typically in the proximal thoracic aorta just beyond the left subclavian artery, next to the opening of the ductus arteriosus"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "May occur alone or with other anomalies: bicuspid aortic valve, VSD, aortic stenosis, PDA, mitral valve disorders, intracerebral aneurysms"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Occurs in 10 to 20% of patients with Turner syndrome"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 6,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Symptoms"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Severe: can present in the neonatal period with acidosis, renal insufficiency and shock; mild: may not be apparent until an adolescent or adult is evaluated for hypertension or diminished femoral pulses"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Typically an "
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       },
       {
        "type": "highlight",
        "attrs": {
         "hex": "FF0000"
        }
       }
      ],
      "text": "upper-to-lower extremity blood pressure gradient"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " and pulse amplitude differential, and a grade 2 to 3/6 ejection systolic murmur, sometimes loudest in the left interscapular area"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "As children age, subtle symptoms may appear (headache, chest pain, fatigue, leg claudication with activity); upper-extremity hypertension is often present"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 0,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": 0,
     "spaceBefore": 6,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": null
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Treatment and next step"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Her chart:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " surgical or balloon repair"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Symptomatic neonates: prostaglandin E1 to reopen the constricted ductus arteriosus"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Correct surgically or by balloon angioplasty with or without stent placement"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
